.TH LISTEN 8
.SH NAME
listen \- announce a service per port, and run its script for each connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B listen
[
.I dir
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Listen
reads
.IR dir ,
.B /lib/service
by default, and announces a TCP port for every file in it named
.BI tcp N,
where
.I N
is the port.
For each connection that arrives it runs the file as an rc script with
the stream as descriptors 0 and 1 and the conversation's directory as
.BR $1 .
.B /lib/service/tcp564
is
.BR "exec exportfs -r /" ;
a new service is a new file.
.PP
One process listens per port.
For each connection it forks a helper, which runs the script and hangs
the conversation up when the script exits, so a finished service leaves
no conversation in the stack's table.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/listen/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR exportfs (4),
.IR srv (4),
.IR import (4)
.SH BUGS
The scripts run as whoever started
.IR listen ,
which is the machine's one user until there are users.
